    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_45e6723c",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts two women in a vintage-style black-and-white photo, with one appearing to be speaking earnestly to the other. The text overlays present two contrasting and extreme statements: the top text warns of eternal damnation for non-believers in God, while the bottom text claims that child abuse isn't necessarily physical. The juxtaposition of these two statements is intentionally jarring and absurd, creating a meme that uses shock value and cognitive dissonance to provoke thought or laughter. The overall intent is not to directly target a specific group with hate, but rather to present a deliberately provocative and potentially harmful message by combining two unrelated and extreme ideas. The meme may be intended to highlight the absurdity of religious dogma or to critique the oversimplification of child abuse, but its presentation can be seen as harmful due to its potential to normalize or trivialize the concept of eternal punishment, and to potentially mislead viewers about the nature of child abuse. The meme's intent is to shock and provoke, but its content can be interpreted as insensitive and potentially damaging to vulnerable individuals or communities.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_6a438358"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
