      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "meme_juxtaposition_technique",
      "label": "Meme Juxtaposition Technique",
      "description": "This is a common meme format where two unrelated or contrasting ideas are placed together to create a humorous, shocking, or thought-provoking effect. The juxtaposition of the theological claim about hell with the statement about child abuse is a deliberate use of this technique to create cognitive dissonance and provoke a reaction from the viewer. Understanding this technique is necessary to interpret the meme's intent.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_6a438358"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_6a4bdb9d",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "religious_fear_mongering",
      "label": "Religious Fear Mongering",
      "description": "The use of threats of eternal punishment to influence belief or behavior is a form of religious fear mongering. This tactic is often used in fundamentalist or evangelical contexts to encourage conversion or adherence to specific doctrines. The meme's inclusion of this concept is meant to highlight or critique the use of fear as a tool in religious discourse.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
